          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: Several people in a vehicle observed on May 17, 2008, around 1:45 a.m., a phenomenon in the sky that intrigued them: two opaque white light masses moved across the sky. They changed shape, appearing and disappearing for a few seconds. Curiosity, piqued by a recent local press article, excellent visibility, and the increasing sophistication of animation lights surprised the witnesses, prompting them to come forward—certainly just a misperception with a Sky Rose-type light. Another witness very likely saw the same thing the following night (case Cesson-Sévigné (35) 5/17/2008). The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of Skyrose-type light animations.",
